	 <note id="GUID-8B731207-59DD-4830-B9D7-C0BE89153617"> 
		<p>All values used for pre-Si estimates and are subject to change. 
		</p> 
		<p><sup>1</sup> Assumes thermally constrained system at steady state (i.e., turbo headroom exhausted) CPU PL1 or combined (CPU+GPU) Power Share PL1 (PSL1) Target @ Tsn limit. 
		</p> 
		<p><sup>2</sup> Narrow VDC (NVDC) has system loss in AC Mode only. Ignore in Battery Mode OR if using alternative PD designs (i.e., Hybrid Power Boost (HPB) or WVDC). 
		</p> 
		<p><sup>3a) 
		  </sup>Assumes 0.5C Charge Rate (example, max charge rates are tightly controlled typically starts ~30% and released/backed-offby ~50% Battery State of Charge). It's maybe possible to manage this to be negligible charging loss with platform management tools like DTT during sustained high concurrency levels. 
		</p> 
		<p><sup>4</sup> Downstream VR Losses are based on improved VR efficiencies by +3% for NVDC versus alternate PD designs. 
		</p> 
		<p><sup>5</sup> For each workload definitions external hardware configurations and application mix detail assumptions, refer to the 
		  <xref scope="local" format="dita" href="GUID-229DBDD9-3185-474B-BF97-82C434E65C09.dita">Section 5.1</xref>. 
		</p> 
	 </note> 
